diff --git a/doc/source/whatsnew/v3.1.0.rst b/doc/source/whatsnew/v3.1.0.rst
index f7bd58a543954..a2852b4afc92a 100644
--- a/doc/source/whatsnew/v3.1.0.rst
+++ b/doc/source/whatsnew/v3.1.0.rst
@@ -1150,6 +1150,7 @@ Sparse
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.any`, :meth:`Series.all`, :meth:`DataFrame.any`, :meth:`DataFrame.all`, :meth:`SparseArray.any`, and :meth:`SparseArray.all` mishandling missing values on :class:`SparseDtype` data: with ``skipna=True`` a missing value was reduced for its own truthiness instead of being skipped, and with ``skipna=False`` missing values were dropped instead of reduced; :meth:`SparseArray.any` and :meth:`SparseArray.all` also raised a ``TypeError`` when called with the ``skipna`` argument (:issue:`68390`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.any`, :meth:`Series.all`, :meth:`DataFrame.any`, :meth:`DataFrame.all`, :meth:`SparseArray.any`, and :meth:`SparseArray.all` returning a result on datetime64 :class:`SparseDtype` data instead of raising ``TypeError`` the way the dense equivalents do (:issue:`68438`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.argmin`, :meth:`Series.argmax`, :meth:`Series.idxmin`, :meth:`Series.idxmax`, :meth:`DataFrame.idxmin`, :meth:`DataFrame.idxmax`, :meth:`SparseArray.argmin`, and :meth:`SparseArray.argmax` raising ``ValueError: attempt to get argmin of an empty sequence`` on :class:`SparseDtype` data with no non-missing stored values, when the non-missing ``fill_value`` occupies at least one position, instead of returning the first such position (:issue:`68462`)
+- Bug in :meth:`Series.astype`, :meth:`DataFrame.astype`, :meth:`Index.astype`, and :meth:`SparseArray.astype` from a :class:`SparseDtype` to a dense dtype silently rounding ``uint64`` values above ``2**53``, and, for a datetime64 or timedelta64 subtype with a boxed :class:`Timestamp` or :class:`Timedelta` ``fill_value``, silently giving wrong values or raising ``TypeError`` (:issue:`68573`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.cumsum`, :meth:`Series.cumprod`, :meth:`Series.cummin`, :meth:`Series.cummax` and their :class:`DataFrame` counterparts raising ``NotImplementedError`` on :class:`SparseDtype` data (:issue:`68187`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.mean` with ``skipna=False`` ignoring missing values for :class:`SparseDtype`-backed :class:`Series` (:issue:`65478`)
 - Bug in :meth:`Series.mean`, :meth:`DataFrame.mean`, and :meth:`SparseArray.mean` on :class:`SparseDtype` data with no non-missing values, an empty array included, emitting a numpy ``RuntimeWarning``, or raising ``ZeroDivisionError`` for an object subtype or ``TypeError`` for a non-numeric ``fill_value``; the missing value is now returned quietly (:issue:`68484`)
